<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110117" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαιός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ά</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>grey,</i> of any colour mixed of black and white, <i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Ti.</u>
				68c
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Cat.</u>
				12a18
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Top.</u>
				106b6
			</span></i>, al.: opp. to both <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλας</span>
			and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκός,</span> in a negative sense,
				<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>R.</u>
				585a
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἄρτοι,</span> opp. to
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λευκοί,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Alex.
				120
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ξανθὸν ἢ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Jul.
					<u>Or.</u>
					4.138d
				</span></i>
			; of mourning, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἱμάτια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					30.4.5
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀποθέσθαι τὰ φ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					15.25.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. ἐσθής</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>SIG</u>
					1219.5
				</span></i>
			 (Gambreion, <span class="entity">iii B.C.</span>)), <i><span class="en">
				D.H.
				5.17
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				D.C.
				49.12
			</span></i>, al.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἰώδης καὶ φ. χολή
				</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">καλοῦσι δ᾽ αὐτὴν
			ἰσατώδη</span>) <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				15.35
			</span></i>; <i>dark-complexioned, P.Strassb.</i><i><span class="en">
				79.2
			</span></i>
			<span class="entity">(i B.C.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of sound, <i>harsh,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Top.</u>
				106b7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Aud.</u>
				802a2
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Poll.
				2.117
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				S.E.
				<u>M.</u>
				6.41
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαιά, ἡ,</span>
			name of a plaster, <i><span class="en">
				Androm.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				13.906
			</span></i>, etc. (Cf. Lith. <i>gaĩsas</i> 'reflected light
			of a blazing fire'.)</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
